anslated. Actionable errors become unstructured HTTP 500 responses.\n  Fix: map access errors to structured 400 responses. Map integration failures to safe 502 responses without response-body logging.\n\n- High: `backend/tests/test_runners_append.py:3-10`.\n  Only missing-bearer behavior is tested. Successful private access, ownership, revoked tokens, malformed input, null results, errors, and consumers remain uncovered.\n  Fix: add endpoint, agent, worker repository, Pi import, Pi sync, and frontend error tests.\n\n### Later improvements\n\n- Medium: `backend/src/yinshi/api/runners.py:289,303-308`.\n  Path uses browser settings namespace instead of established runner control namespace. Response keys also abbreviate canonical field names.\n  Fix: use `/runner/github-access` and typed fields such as `installation_id` and `repository_installation_id`.\n\n- Medium: `backend/src/yinshi/api/runners.py:34-46` and `backend/src/yinshi/models.py:445-457`.\n  Duplicate request models exist. Shared model is unused. Extra request fields are silently ignored.\n  Fix: keep one strict model with `extra=\"forbid\"` and add a typed response model.\n\n- Medium: `backend/src/yinshi/api/runners.py:31-58`.\n  Import placement, unused imports, and formatting fail Black, isort, and flake8.\n  Fix: normalize imports, remove unused names, and format changed files.\n\n- Note: Requested `plan.md` and `progress.md` were absent.\n- Note: No files were edited, staged, committed, pushed, or deployed.",
